  "applies_to": "ABB SACE PR122DC and PR123DC DC protection trip units with the PR120/D-M communication module, document rev 02 (04/04/2014, SW 3.01 and later).",
  "summary": "The PR122DC and PR123DC are the DC versions of ABB's Emax trip units. With the PR120/D-M module they talk Modbus RTU: pole currents, DC voltage, power and energy are input registers, and commands such as open, close and trip reset are written to two holding registers. 32-bit values are sent low word first.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The map gives relative addresses on 30001 (input registers, function 4) and 40001 (holding registers) bases; its example says run-time measures at offset 200 are 30201, relative address 200, which is the wire address with 'Standard' addressing."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": "SW 3.01 and later",
  "source": {
    "title": "Communication System Interface for protection trip units PR122DC and PR123DC + PR120/D-M Com module",
    "doc_number": "1SDH000841R0001 rev 02",
    "revision_date": "2014-04-04",
    "url": "https://library.e.abb.com/public/14a57dd39209c59dc12578b100664838/1SDH000841R0001.pdf",
    "pages": "Comms parameters p. 5; Modbus map and word order pp. 9-10; commands p. 13; state pp. 16-18; run-time measures p. 19; information p. 20"
  },
  "notes": [
    "The document states 4-byte values are sent with the low word at the lower address (LOW-HIGH), bytes within a word high first, so 32-bit registers are CDAB.",
    "External bus settings: 9600 or 19200 baud, address 1-247, Standard or ABB addressing, E,8,1 / O,8,1 / N,8,2 / N,8,1. The document does not state the external-bus factory values.",
    "IB, IB_2, ground current, voltage, power and energy are PR123DC only.",
    "Left out: state words other than 2 and 8, statistics, history, logger and parameter areas.",
    "Over the external bus, commands are accepted only in Remote mode (state 2 bit 9)."
  ],
